00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.400
What's the matter?

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.440
Huh?

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:28.060
There's something on your mind, I can tell.

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:29.020
Yeah.

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:32.520
It's about Miss Mana...

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:37.440
You know, I'm not intentionally
trying to sound like Miss Mana.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.900
I'm only singing naturally...

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.600
Well...

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:46.560
I was suddenly able to sing
like this after my surgery.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.650
I'm not especially concerned.

00:13:48.650 --> 00:13:52.100
Just sing with your voice as usual, Sakura.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:07.850
I put together a schedule for here on out.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:11.850
Start practice at the studio
in Tokyo at six in the morning.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.520
Until 10 at night?!

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:17.900
Even the first train won't get us
there in time for the 6 AM start!

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:21.980
Suzu's the one who said we won't win
the finals if we don't step things up.

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:25.690
We need to tackle the finals
in an entirely different way!

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:29.020
This voice...

00:14:29.020 --> 00:14:30.440
Sakura?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.150
What did you think of that?

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:38.900
Yeah... That didn't sound
like Miss Mana just now.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.230
Really?

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.100
But...

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.650
Sakura.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.520
Kotono.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:49.190
You weren't singing like
you normally would just now.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:54.060
Sakura wanted to try out
a different way to sing.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:55.350
But why?

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.190
Because...

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:04.770
Let's talk just the two of us for a second.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.730
The thing is...

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:11.600
I researched about Miss Mana last night.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:13.600
About my sister?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.690
Yup.

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:18.150
Where she was born,
how she became an idol...

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.480
How popular she was...

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:24.770
You know, I was never too
knowledgeable about those things.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.400
Okay.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.520
I watched her footage...

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.690
She really was amazing.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:33.060
I've seen them a few times before,

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:36.560
but I was amazed again re-watching them.

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:41.480
I feel bad that people say I remind them of her.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:44.900
And now you're trying to change your singing?

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:47.230
When you've been advancing with that voice?

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.310
Is it going to work changing it so suddenly?

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:54.600
Tell me the truth.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:55.940
Sakura.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.350
"Sakura Kawasaki, Return of Mana Nagase?"
"Sakura Kawasaki, the leader of Sunny Peace from
Hoshimi Productions that made it as a finalist
in the current Next Venus Grand Prix..."

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.980
When I asked Shizuku...

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:12.690
She told me people would call me the successor
of Miss Mana if I kept singing the way I am now.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:16.150
I questioned whether you would
be okay with that, Kotono.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:18.350
I thought you wouldn't like that.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:21.480
I don't mind.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.900
Really?

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:26.520
Kotono, aren't you singing for Miss Mana?

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.400
Tell me the truth!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:38.690
I don't have my sister's voice.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:41.190
I'm not as talented a singer as her.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:44.350
I can't move the audience as much as her.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.730
That's not true!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.440
It is so!

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:52.020
No matter how much I practice, I fail.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:54.440
Even if I sing in place of my sister,

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:57.850
I won't be able to dispel her regret.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.190
But you're different, Sakura!

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.980
You can make it happen.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.350
Kotono...

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:05.810
Sakura...

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:08.600
You could sing the song my sister
was supposed to sing at the finals...

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.600
What?

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:13.560
I want you to sing it, Sakura.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.810
"Rio Kanzaki of LizNoir...
I feel a great energy from her.
How can I describe it... Hunger?"

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.480
Yes.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.230
Kotono, can we talk a bit?

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.270
Did something happen between you and Sakura?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:32.690
Huh?

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.190
You both are so easy to read.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:39.230
You both have avoided eye contact with
each other ever since practice ended.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:41.350
I let Sakura know...

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.400
...that she shouldn't mind me

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.100
and keep singing the way she's been.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.100
I see.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:53.690
I've always felt that I needed to reach
the top as an idol in place of my sister.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:58.850
But... I just can't sing like my sister.

00:17:58.850 --> 00:18:02.230
That's when Sakura appeared, right?

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:03.060
Yup.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:07.150
I believe Sakura will be able
to sing like my sister.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:10.020
But if that's the case,

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:13.480
I don't know why I'm participating
in the Grand Prix.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.810
I see.

00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:19.900
I know I can't be like this.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.400
Everyone's putting their all
into the Grand Prix.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:26.520
It'd be disrespectful if I
didn't put in my all, too.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.560
I think you should do
as you want to, Kotono.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:32.230
As for me and everyone,

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:36.150
I think we all understand
how you feel, Kotono.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.850
Really?

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:38.770
Yup.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:42.190
We noticed something was wrong recently...

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.560
Maybe you were struggling with something...

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.520
Mei, Suzu, and Saki were worried, too!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.900
W-Was I really acting that strange?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.060
No, it's not like that.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.900
Since we've been working together all this time,

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:58.650
we're able to sense even
the most subtle changes.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:00.100
Everyone did...?

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.060
I'm sorry.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:05.900
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.190
Suzu- <i>nyan</i> made us do it!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:12.230
Hold up, you're the one
who instigated this, Mei!

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:15.650
Anyway, we all care about you.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:20.650
To be honest, I don't really know
anything about Miss Mana.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:26.690
I just know I'd be happy leaving a good record
in the Grand Prix singing with you, Kotono.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.900
Me, too!

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.350
Really?

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:30.770
Yup!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:34.810
Everyone loves your singing, Kotono.

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:39.230
Regardless of Miss Mana, we all want
to sing together with you, Kotono!

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:44.020
But my singing is...
Compared to my sister's...

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:48.560
You cannot compare yourself
with Miss Mana!

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.940
I-It's just...

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:53.600
It's true that you have your
own good qualities, too!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.440
Suzu.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.940
If you're feeling lost without a goal,

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.270
just think that you're doing it for all of us.

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.730
For all of you?

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.810
We've worked so hard together.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:11.400
It would not hurt to do that for us.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:12.810
For everyone...

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:17.400
That's right, we, Moon Tempest,
will sing for all of us.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:21.060
We'll aim for the top of
the Grand Prix for all of us.

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:23.690
That is usually the case, you know?

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:27.150
So if you can think that way, too, Kotono...

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:32.270
With all of us who think your voice...
who think your singing is the best!

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:33.730
Together!

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:42.730
Thanks.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:48.310
I was fixated on my sister and had no clue...

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:52.350
I didn't know that's how
you all felt about me...

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.400
And the group...

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.520
It's a blessing from the moon.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:05.560
Yup.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:08.150
I'm going to aim to win...

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:10.480
...with Moon Tempest.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.100
With everyone here!

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.850
We were shown the overwhelming strength

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:23.600
of the likely winner, LizNoir,
in the first battle of the first round!

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:27.400
The second battle is between
Moon Tempest and Krystal!

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:31.310
Now, which group will the
goddess of victory smile upon?

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.150
Let the performance begin!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:38.560
Now, let's sing!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.310
From here to the future!

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:41.980
From here to space!

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.730
Let's aim for the top!

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:46.900
With the light of the moon in our hands!

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:48.810
Moon Tempest!

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:26.480
Kotono!

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:27.520
Yay!

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:30.230
Hey! Nagisa, Suzu, Mei...

00:23:30.230 --> 00:23:31.770
Then me, too!

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:33.310
Um...

00:23:33.310 --> 00:23:36.150
Come on, just for today.

00:23:36.150 --> 00:23:37.850
Amazing!

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:47.150
You're Good Just the Way You Are
